    "id": "N10-009-C01-Q081",
    "chapterIndex": 0,
    "text": "Scenario: A network technician is troubleshooting a PC that has no connectivity. He notices that the network icon has a red \"X\". He swaps the patch cable, but the icon stays the same. He then plugs the PC into a different wall jack, but the problem persists. He decides to look at the network card itself and notices the physical RJ-45 port pins inside are bent and touching each other. Which troubleshooting step has he just completed, and what layer is the fault located at?",
